Junior Web Developer
Department: Software Engineering
Entry-level
Full-time
0–2 years




Job Summary
We are seeking a Junior Web Developer to build, maintain, and improve responsive web applications. The candidate should understand frontend development, possess basic backend programming knowledge, and be comfortable working with databases and version-control systems.
Key Responsibilities
- Develop responsive and user-friendly web pages using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
- Build reusable frontend components and implement interactive user interfaces.
- Develop backend routes, APIs, and application logic using Python and Flask or a similar framework.
- Integrate web applications with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL.
- Validate user input and implement appropriate error handling.
- Test and debug applications across different browsers and screen sizes.
- Use Git and GitHub to manage source code and collaborate with team members.
- Maintain existing applications, fix bugs, and improve performance.
- Follow coding standards and document application features and implementation details.
Required Skills
- Frontend: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, responsive design, and DOM manipulation.
- Backend: Python fundamentals and experience with Flask, Django, Node.js, or a similar framework.
- Database: SQL fundamentals and CRUD operations.
- Version control: Git, GitHub, branching, and basic collaboration workflows.
- Web fundamentals: HTTP requests, REST APIs, JSON, and client-server architecture.
- Debugging: Browser developer tools, error analysis, and systematic problem-solving.
- Soft skills: Communication, teamwork, adaptability, and willingness to learn.
Educational Qualifications
- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.
- Equivalent practical experience through personal projects, internships, or academic assignments is also valuable.
Preferred Skills
- Familiarity with React or another JavaScript frontend framework.
- Experience with authentication and user-session management.
- Understanding of application deployment and environment variables.
- Familiarity with automated testing and software development practices.
- Experience building full-stack academic or personal projects.
Example Success Criteria
- Deliver responsive, functional, and maintainable web applications.
- Build reliable integrations between frontend interfaces, backend services, and databases.
- Resolve reported bugs and improve application usability.